  "holistic_F_N": -1,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires reporting of all listed thermal incidents within 24 hours and customer notice within 72 hours, which is strict. S2 keeps the 5% limit and gives customers per-model numerical results while keeping them non-public, but the existing-model corrective period is 'reasonable' with no fixed end. S5 sets the 8/100k threshold as a trigger for notification and assessment, not an automatic recall, so recall is left to regulator discretion. Parameter extraction for S5 assumes recall_mandatory=false and permanent_trigger=null, since no recall is mandatory at the threshold; the 8/100k figure appears only as a notification trigger."
